# T-07 (V-04): the contracted LAST-STEP failure — H1 is created then
# destroyed by the ORIGINAL provider before -3; EVERY caller byte stays
# untouched (the frozen failure transport, exit 70). The full allocation-
# domain fault sweep (V-05: k=1..N, N+1 no-op, clear+same-process retry,
# ledger balance) rides the ace-abi conformance leg
# (resource939_fault_sweep.c) — the fallible failure transport ends the
# source program, so the sweep cannot live in a deck.
```test-case
case { schema: "autolang.case/2", id: "ace-ca-d3.txn3-lastfail-native", tags: ["ca-d3", "certify"],
